10 REM 10 PRINT -- COOL8 EDITION
20 REM AFTER THE C64 ONE-LINER:
30 REM 10 PRINT CHR$(205.5+RND(1)); : GOTO 10
40 REM
50 REM PETSCII 205 AND 206 REACH THE CELL CORNERS, SO THE
60 REM MAZE JOINS UP. OUR FONT IS CP437 AND ITS / AND \
70 REM HAVE SIDE BEARING -- THEY STOP SHORT, AND THE MAZE
80 REM BREAKS AT EVERY CELL EDGE. THE TEXT FONT IS ROM,
90 REM SO THE FIX IS TILE MODE, WHERE THE PATTERN IS RAM.
100 REM MODE 2 IS 40X30 LIKE MODE 1: CELLS ARE SQUARE.
110 REM ONE TILE SERVES BOTH DIAGONALS -- BIT 6 FLIPS IT.
120 MODE 2
130 FOR I=0 TO 15
140 POKE $FF1E,I:READ R,G:POKE $FF1F,R:POKE $FF1F,G
150 NEXT
160 DATA 0,0,15,255,8,0,10,254
170 DATA 12,76,0,197,0,10,14,231
180 DATA 13,133,6,64,15,119,3,51
190 DATA 7,119,10,246,0,143,11,187
200 REM PATTERNS AT $4000; TILE 1 IS AT $4020.
210 POKE $FF20,0:POKE $FF21,$40
220 POKE $FF26,$20:POKE $FF27,$40:POKE $FF28,1
230 REM SCREEN CODE 77 OUT OF THE C64 CHARACTER ROM,
240 REM PIXEL FOR PIXEL, AT 4BPP: PAPER 6, INK 14. IT IS
250 REM TWO AND THREE PIXELS WIDE, NOT ONE, AND IT MEETS
260 REM BOTH CORNERS -- WHICH IS WHY THE MAZE JOINS UP.
270 REM CODE 78 IS ITS EXACT MIRROR, SO BIT 6 IS ENOUGH.
280 FOR I=1 TO 32:READ D:POKE $FF29,D:NEXT
290 DATA 238,102,102,102,238,230,102,102
300 DATA 110,238,102,102,102,238,230,102
310 DATA 102,110,238,102,102,102,238,230
320 DATA 102,102,110,238,102,102,102,238
330 REM THE SCROLL IS THE HARDWARE'S: NOTHING MOVES IN
340 REM MEMORY. THE MAP IS A RING 32 ROWS TALL WITH 30
350 REM SHOWN, $FF18 IS THE FINE STEP INSIDE A TILE, AND
360 REM THE COARSE STEP IS ONE STRIDE ONTO VID_BASE.
365 REM $FF1D BIT 1 IS THE VBLANK FLAG: WRITE 1 TO CLEAR
366 REM IT, THEN WAIT FOR IT. ONE FRAME, UNAMBIGUOUSLY --
367 REM VID_RASTER CANNOT DO THIS, ITS COUNT IS 8 BITS OF
368 REM A LINE NUMBER THAT RUNS PAST 255.
369 REM THE WRAP IS A COMPARE AND SUBTRACT, NOT A MASK:
370 REM THE MAP HAS AN ORIGIN REGISTER OF ITS OWN, SO ANY
371 REM STRIDE AND ANY ADDRESS WORK. TEXT'S OWN 160 IS NOT
372 REM A POWER OF TWO, AND IT SCROLLS.
373 M=PEEK($FF12)+PEEK($FF13)*256
374 S=PEEK($FF14)+PEEK($FF15)*256
380 W=S*32:P=M:B=M:N=0
390 FOR C=0 TO 39
400 A=P+C*2
410 POKE $FF26,A AND 255
420 POKE $FF27,A/256
430 POKE $FF29,1
440 POKE $FF29,RND(2)*64
450 NEXT
460 P=P+S:IF P>=M+W THEN P=P-W
465 N=N+1
470 IF N<31 THEN GOTO 390
471 REM BOTH VID_BASE AND THE TILE ROW ARE SAMPLED AT
472 REM FRAME START, AND THE VBLANK FLAG SETS THERE TOO --
473 REM SO EVERYTHING WRITTEN AFTER SEEING IT LANDS ON THE
474 REM NEXT FRAME, BOTH ALIKE. THE BASE THEREFORE GOES
475 REM WITH FINE STEP 0, NOT WITH 7: PAIR IT WITH 7 AND
476 REM ONE FRAME SHOWS A ROW AND SEVEN PIXELS AT ONCE,
477 REM THEN COMES BACK. THAT IS THE SHUDDER.
479 REM TWO TICKS A STEP, NOT ONE. FORTY CELLS A TILE ROW
480 FOR F=0 TO 7
481 FOR V=0 TO 1
482 POKE $FF1D,2
484 IF (PEEK($FF1D) AND 2)=0 THEN GOTO 484
485 NEXT
486 IF F=0 THEN B=B+S
487 IF F=0 THEN IF B>=M+W THEN B=B-W
488 IF F=0 THEN POKE $FF12,B AND 255
489 IF F=0 THEN POKE $FF13,B/256
490 POKE $FF18,F
492 REM A FIFTH OF THE NEXT ROW PER FRAME: FORTY CELLS
493 REM WILL NOT FIT IN ONE, AND A ROW DRAWN ALL AT ONCE
494 REM STALLS THE SCROLL FOR AS LONG AS IT TAKES.
495 FOR C=F*5 TO F*5+4
496 A=P+C*2
497 POKE $FF26,A AND 255:POKE $FF27,A/256
498 POKE $FF29,1:POKE $FF29,RND(2)*64
499 NEXT
500 NEXT
501 P=P+S:IF P>=M+W THEN P=P-W
502 GOTO 480
